This Agreement is entered into between **CSMT** (“Party One”) and **Volvo** (“Party Two”) concerning the development
and use of software code-named **“Volvo FaceM.”** The purpose of Volvo FaceM is to develop and implement a vehicle-based
facial detection and driver drowsiness monitoring system designed to detect signs of driver fatigue, reduced alertness,
or drowsiness and support improved driving safety. Both parties agree that all software, source code, algorithms, models,
technical documentation, data, designs, and related information associated with Volvo FaceM shall be treated as confidential
and shall be used solely for the purposes agreed upon between CSMT and Volvo. Neither party shall sell, license, disclose,
transfer, share, distribute, provide access to, or otherwise make the Volvo FaceM software or its associated confidential
information available to any other company, organization, government authority, individual, or third party without the
prior written consent of the other party, except where disclosure is strictly required by applicable law. Any use, testing,
verification, evaluation, or modification of Volvo FaceM by an external party shall likewise require prior written approval
from both CSMT and Volvo. This Agreement is intended to establish a confidential, two-party relationship between CSMT and Volvo
for the development, evaluation, and use of Volvo FaceM.



